    "label": "thm:ETC-K",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Fix $K\\ge 2$ and $m\\le T/K$. For the Explore-Then-Commit algorithm $\\mbox{ETC}_m$ (which explores each arm $m$ times and then commits), the worst-case regret with a single breakpoint satisfies $\\Rwc(\\mbox{ETC}_m)\\ge T - m \\ge (1-1/K)T$ (when $m\\le T/K$)."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Also implies >= (1-1/K)T. Regret is dynamic pseudo-regret worst-cased over one-breakpoint instances."
  },
